      "end_timestamp": "03:44",
      "supports": [
        "vital_signs[0]",
        "vital_signs[1]",
        "vital_signs[2]",
        "vital_signs[3]",
        "vital_signs[4]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "There are crackles at the right base and the breathing is a bit fast.",
      "start_timestamp": "04:17",
      "end_timestamp": "04:23",
      "supports": [
        "physical_examination[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "So where does that leave us? I'm honestly not certain yet. It could be community-acquired pneumonia, or it might be acute bronchitis.",
      "start_timestamp": "04:43",
      "end_timestamp": "04:53",
      "supports": [
        "clinical_assessment[0]",
        "clinical_assessment[1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "I can't promise yet, but most people with community-acquired pneumonia do well once it's treated properly.",
      "start_timestamp": "04:59",
      "end_timestamp": "05:05",
      "supports": [
        "clinical_assessment[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Let's get a chest X-ray, for possible pneumonia. I'm going to order blood tests, for pneumonia. The treatment will be amoxicillin, 500 milligrams, three times a day, five days. You take it by mouth. It's for chest infection. It's a commonly used medicine and most people tolerate it well.",
      "start_timestamp": "05:16",
      "end_timestamp": "05:39",
      "supports": [
        "medications[1]",
        "procedures_and_investigations[0]",
        "procedures_and_investigations[1]",
